From d093bdf49813640e99ebf15e045551dbe6b9c787 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei Vladescu <52881237+AndreiVladescu@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 21:34:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mediatek: filogic: add support for TP-Link Deco X55 v3

Hardware:
 - SoC:      MediaTek MT7981B, 2x Cortex-A53 @ 1.3 GHz
 - RAM:      512 MiB DDR3
 - Flash:    128 MiB SPI-NAND
 - Ethernet: 2x 1GbE via MT7531 switch (LAN), 1x 1GbE via MT7981 internal PHY (WAN)
 - Wi-Fi:    MT7981 2x2 2.4 GHz + 2x2 5 GHz (802.11ax, HE160), ePA/eLNA
 - LED:      one RGB status LED (red GPIO 9, green GPIO 12, blue GPIO 28)
 - Button:   reset (GPIO 1)

The OEM boot chain is kept: TP-Link U-Boot loads the UBI volume "uboot"
(TP-Link's "seconduboot") from the slot selected by tp_boot_idx, which then
boots FIT configuration "config-X50_3_0_0" from volume "kernel". OpenWrt is
installed into ubi0 with the OEM second U-Boot as static volume 0; ubi1 keeps
the stock firmware as a fallback.

Wi-Fi calibration and the base MAC are files inside the UBIFS volume
"ubi_factory_data" (same scheme as the Mercusys H90X), mounted read-only
in preinit. MAC addresses follow the stock scheme:
LAN = base, WAN = base + 1, 2.4 GHz = base + 2, 5 GHz = base + 3.

Installation (from the OEM firmware, needs UART):
 1. interrupt the OEM U-Boot, TFTP-boot the initramfs image:
      tftpboot 0x50000000 <initramfs-kernel.bin>
      bootm 0x50000000#config-X50_3_0_0
 2. sysupgrade with the sysupgrade image. This replaces kernel/rootfs in
    slot ubi0, keeps the OEM "uboot" volume there and sets tp_boot_idx=0.
 Revert to the OEM firmware in ubi1: fw_setenv tp_boot_idx 1

Tested on two units: flash boot through the OEM chain, Ethernet/DSA,
MACs, caldata, Wi-Fi (HE160 2x2, 2401.9 Mbit/s PHY), WED + PPE offload,
LED, reset button, sysupgrade with and without kept settings.

Signed-off-by: Andrei Vladescu <52881237+AndreiVladescu@users.noreply.github.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
